","numeric":11}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-040357","Abbreviation_in_the_article":2,"Cell_line":"RD","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"2.5 ± 0.9","IC50_Dark_value":2.5,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1016/j.cbi.2023.110742","Year":2023,"Counterion":"O=S(=O)([O-])C(F)(F)F","Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-040357","value":"5 ± 2","numeric":5}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-040358","Abbreviation_in_the_article":2,"Cell_line":"HepG2","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"24 ± 3","IC50_Dark_value":24,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1016/j.cbi.2023.110742","Year":2023,"Counterion":"O=S(=O)([O-])C(F)(F)F","Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-040358","value":"11 ± 3","numeric":11}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-040359","Abbreviation_in_the_article":2,"Cell_line":"MRC-5","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"39 ± 20","IC50_Dark_value":39,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1016/j.cbi.2023.110742","Year":2023,"Counterion":"O=S(=O)([O-])C(F)(F)F","Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-040359","value":"8 ± 2","numeric":8}}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":2,"value":0.14,"value_relation":"=","std":0.02,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","temperature_C":21,"doi":"10.1016/j.cbi.2023.110742","year":2023,"counterion":"O=S(=O)([O-])C(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-003364","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"Partition coefficients (Log Pow), defined as Pow = corg/caq, where corg and caq are molar concentrations of the selected compound in the n-octanol and aqueous phase, respectively, were determined by the shake-flask method and UV–Vis measurements as previously reported [75,76]. Thus, deionized water and 1-octanol were vigorously stirred for 24 h to allow saturation of both phases. A stock solution of the selected diiron complex (ca. 2 mg) was prepared by first adding acetone (50 μL to assist solubilization), followed by water-saturated octanol (3.0 mL). The solution was diluted with water-saturated octanol (ca. 1:3 v/v ratio, cFe2 ≈ 10-4 M, so that 1.5 ≤ A ≤ 2.0 at 340 nm), and thus the UV–Vis spectrum was recorded (A0org). An aliquot of the non-diluted solution (Vorg = 1.2 mL) was transferred into a test tube, and octanol-saturated water (Vorg = Vaq = 1.2 mL) was added. The mixture was vigorously stirred for 30 min at room temperature (ca. 21 °C) and then centrifuged (5000 rpm, 5 min). The UV–Vis spectrum of the organic phase was recorded (Aforg), and the partition coefficient was calculated as Pow = Aforg/(A0org - Aforg), where A0org and Aforg are the absorbance values in the organic phase before and after partition with the aqueous phase, respectively. The procedure was repeated three times for each sample (from the same stock solution); results are given as mean ± standard deviation (Table 1)."}]}